    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's an interesting way to look at it. the \"prankster\" idea helps. \n\nbut what i mean is, when it gets really bad—like when you're fighting a heavy crosswind or feeling that sudden drop in lift—it doesn't really feel like a \"spirited goat.\" it feels more like something is actively trying to trip me up or mess with my controls. \n\nlike, if you had to give that \"mischievousness\" a more specific form, something that actually has intent behind it, what would it be? like, if the air is \"acting up,\" what kind of little creature or entity is actually doing the disrupting?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
